    "/**\n   * The last card of the target column, in document order — the place a card with no pivot lands.\n   * Either the column's true last card, or one standing somewhere before it: a pivot can land a card\n   * mid-document, so a read may still have to walk forward to find where the column ends.\n   */",
    "/** Where the card lands, read off the list without it, the way the array mover reads the array. */",
    "// A pivot only names a place inside a column that still has cards: the array mover never",
    "// reached it when the target group came out empty, and the card went to the document's end.",
